      {
        "id": "p24-p2-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Estimate the **mode** and **median** from your graphs.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Modal class: 10–14 hours. Estimated median: 12.5 hours.",
          "worked": "The tallest histogram bar is the 10–14 hours class, with frequency $15$.\n\nFor the median, use cumulative frequency $50\\div 2=25$. Read across from $25$ to the polygon and then down to about $12.5$ hours.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 16
      },
      {
        "id": "p25-p2-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Compare how well these estimates match calculations from the grouped frequency table.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Both methods give the modal class 10–14 hours. The table places the median in that class, and linear interpolation gives 12.5 hours, matching the polygon estimate.",
          "worked": "The largest class frequency is $15$, so the table and histogram give the same modal class, 10–14 hours. The cumulative frequencies before and after that class are $16$ and $31$. The 25th and 26th values are both in that class.\n\nEstimating within the class in the same way as the polygon gives\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Estimated median} &= 9.5+5\\times\\frac{25-16}{31-16}\\\\\\text{Estimated median} &= 12.5\\text{ hours}.\\end{align*}$$\nThe match follows because the polygon uses straight segments between the class boundaries. The exact median requires the original data.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 19
      }
    ]
